[1;38;2;239;68;90m│[0m [38;2;232;240;255m[1;38;2;242;198;94mOrchestrator[38;2;232;240;255m runs your conversation in a [1;38;2;242;198;94mtwo-phase plan-and-execute workflow[38;2;232;240;255m using two different models instead of one:[0m
[1;38;2;239;68;90m│[0m [38;2;232;240;255m[0m
[1;38;2;239;68;90m│[0m [38;2;232;240;255m1. [1;38;2;242;198;94mPlanning phase (stronger model):[38;2;232;240;255m Every message you send starts here. For tasks that require changes or actions, the planner investigates read-only (reading files, searching, inspecting outputs), makes design and implementation decisions, and creates a concrete step-by-step plan.[0m
[1;38;2;239;68;90m│[0m [38;2;232;240;255m2. [1;38;2;242;198;94mExecution phase (faster, lighter model):[38;2;232;240;255m Once the plan is ready, the planner hands off to a faster, lower-cost execution model within the same conversation to actually make the edits, run commands, and verify the results.[0m
[1;38;2;239;68;90m│[0m [38;2;232;240;255m3. [1;38;2;242;198;94mReview & hand-back:[38;2;232;240;255m If the execution model runs into something unexpected, needs a decision, reaches a review point, or you send a follow-up message mid-task, control returns to the planning model to review progress and update the plan.[0m
[1;38;2;239;68;90m│[0m [38;2;232;240;255m4. [1;38;2;242;198;94mDirect answers for questions:[38;2;232;240;255m When your request doesn't require edits or external actions (like asking a question or reviewing code), the planning model simply answers directly without handing off.[0m
[1;38;2;239;68;90m│[0m [38;2;232;240;255m[0m
[1;38;2;239;68;90m│[0m [38;2;232;240;255m[1;38;2;242;198;94mIn short:[38;2;232;240;255m It combines the reasoning strength of a flagship model for planning and hard decisions with the speed and efficiency of a lighter model for carrying out the work.[0m
[1;38;2;239;68;90m╰────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────[0m

